### Crash Recovery: run the release under an ID you own
### Start the app first: diagrid dev run -f dev-crash-test.yaml --approve
### "kill_after_seconds": 8 makes the app halt itself 8s into turn 2 (the release
### checks), so you do not need the kill request below. Restarting the app is what
### recovers the run; send this exact request again only to read back its answer,
### because the crash killed the connection that was waiting for one.
### Remove "kill_after_seconds" (and use a new id) to crash the app yourself with
### the request below while turn 2 runs (~10s).
POST http://localhost:8001/crash/run
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "id": "release-42",
    "prompt": "Write release notes for version 2.5.0 to RELEASE_NOTES.md: it adds offline mode and fixes the CSV export crash.",
    "kill_after_seconds": 8
}

### Crash Recovery: kill the app while the run above is in flight
POST http://localhost:8001/crash/kill
